# Repository-wide ignores for Projects-Git.
#
# Each project may also carry its own .gitignore (PythonHotel does). Git reads
# every .gitignore it finds on the way down, so a rule here applies everywhere
# and a rule in a project's own file applies to that project only. Both are
# in force at the same time.

# ---- projects not ready to be published yet ------------------------------
# Excluded on purpose for now. Delete this line to start tracking it.
PythonStocks/

# ---- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments are machine-specific: they hardcode absolute paths to
# the folder and to the interpreter they were built from, so a copied one
# breaks. Each machine recreates its own (PythonHotel: ./setup.sh).
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# ---- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit real credentials. PythonHotel's hotels.json is deliberately
# NOT ignored (the keys in it are published in each hotel's own "Book Now"
# link), but anything matching these stays out.
.env
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json
